# Section spacing

Every major page section uses **10px margin-top** and **10px margin-bottom** on its outer `<section>` only. This is the permanent standard unless the user specifies otherwise.

## How to apply

- Shared sections: `src/components/Section.astro` already adds `.page-section`. Do not add a second margin.
- Raw outer `<section>` elements: add `page-section`.
- Rule: `.page-section` in `src/styles/global.css`.
- `main` is a column flex container when it directly contains `.page-section`, so adjacent 10px margins do not collapse. The visible gap between two sections is 20px.

## Do not

- Change section padding (`py-section`, `--section-padding-y`, or component padding).
- Change internal spacing of headings, paragraphs, cards, buttons, or other nested elements.
- Put `.page-section` on nested sections, cards, or components.
- Use a broad `section` selector.

## Exceptions

- Heroes under the fixed header (`Hero`, `PageHero`, `LocationHero`, `ServiceHero`) also use `page-section--flush-top` (`margin-top: 0`). A top margin would show the page background above the full-bleed hero. Their bottom margin stays 10px.
- `WhatHappensNext` keeps `margin-bottom: 0`. Its full-bleed map is a sibling meant to sit flush under the section and against the footer. Top margin stays 10px.
